                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i1">               
                            <locus from="1r" to="74r"/>
                            <title>History of Ethiopia and the Catholics</title>
                            <note>Collection of historical accounts by <persName ref="PRS12520TaklaH"/> regarding the political and religious 
                                history of Eritrea and the Ethiopian Highlands. It relies primarily on traditional sources such as chronological lists and 
                                the <ref type="work" corresp="LIT2375Synaxa"/>, yet displays a greater degree of originality from the reign of
                                <persName ref="PRS10303Yekunno"/> (from <locus target="#21v"/>) onwards and becomes more detailed for the 
                                period starting in the <date notBefore="1820" notAfter="1829">1820ies</date> (from <locus target="25r"/>). The 
                                historical accounts end with the suicide of  <persName ref="PRS9430Tewodros"/> at <placeName ref="LOC4547Maqdal"/>
                                in <date when="1868">1868</date>. The text is divided into 31 chapters of varying lengths, the beginnings of which are
                                not marked in the first ten chapters. A large part of the narrative on <locus from="25r" to="74r"/> deals with the life story
                                of <persName ref="PRS3451DeJacob"/>, whom the author knew well. A considerable number of the details presented 
                                in this document were set forth by this missionary in <bibl><ptr target="bm:TaklaHaymanot1914Jacobis"/></bibl>.  
                                See also <ref type="work" corresp="LIT5354Mashaf"/> in <ref type="mss" corresp="ANLcr79"/> by the same author.
                                For the larger part of the treatise from <locus from="19v1" to="74r"/>, an Italian translation was published by 
                                <persName ref="PRS3182ContiRo"/> in <bibl><ptr target="bm:ContiRossini1916Fonti"/></bibl>. In the preface to
                                this translation on page 425 to 427, there is a description of this document and its author.</note>
